# Study copies of decompiled projects. Read only. Never committed, never shipped, never read at runtime.
knowledge/study/

# Generated from data\ by tools\sync_data.py. The source of truth is data\, not this mirror.
game/datafiles/

# game\art retired on 2026-10-23 (card t_4e54cc9e). The sprite queue measures game\sprites_src, which
# is the authored tree, and tools\sync_art.py rebuilds game\datafiles\art from it, which is what the
# game reads. This line and the comment block above it are kept in git history, not here, because an
# ignore rule for a folder that no longer exists is how a retired path keeps coming back.

# Build output and per user IDE state.
build/
*.yyz
*.resource_order
game/.resource_order

# Igor build products and its cache. Measured 2026-10-21: output/ held 17 untracked files
# including PrimordialParadox.exe (7.9 MB) and PrimordialParadox.win, and the repo root
# .gitignore did not cover them, so a build would have committed 8 MB of binary.
#
# The review previews below stay tracked. tests/test_make_env_ship.py,
# tests/test_make_title_world.py and tests/test_sfx.py assert they exist and call them "the
# picture the manager reviews", so a clean checkout must have them. Note the exclusion is
# output/* and not output/: git never descends into an excluded directory, so a negation
# under output/ would be a dead line, which is exactly how the title theme MIDI exceptions
# silently did nothing earlier.
output/*
# tests/test_palette_synergy.py measures this frame through palette_synergy.py by path, so a
# clean checkout must carry it: the test used to skip when it was absent, which is the silent
# pass tests/test_test_inputs.py now forbids. Written by tools/art/scene_palette.py.
!output/nes_title_frame.png
!output/env_ship_preview.png
!output/nes_ui_preview.png
!output/title_ui_preview.png
!output/ts2_world_preview.png
!output/ts2_bigben_preview.png
!output/sfx_preview_3x.png
!output/render2_demo_preview.png
!output/scene_palettes.json
# Three frames that tracked tests read by path and three judged rows name as the ground they measure, and
# that no commit carried. Card t_19b41ab7, measured 2026-10-25: a clean checkout of 5f290c5 reported
# "3 failed, 33 passed" on tests/test_palette_synergy.py and tests/test_scene_palette_set.py while this
# working tree reported 1529 passed, because output/* excluded all three and tests/test_test_inputs.py did
# not name them. They are readings, not decoration, and each one is written by a tool, so none of them is a
# pasted picture:
#   output/cloud_sky_ground.png            tools/art/title_cloud_ground.py, the 48x16 crop of title_L1_sky
#                                          frame 0 at y 80 (the composer's CLOUD_DY) that the cloud is read on
#   output/bg_battle_corridor_frame.png    tools/art/make_battle_bg.py, the corridor strip in a 256x240 frame
#   output/bg_battle_deck_night_frame.png  tools/art/make_battle_bg.py, the deck strip in the same frame
# Per file, after output/*, for the reason above: the folder itself is excluded, so a rule for a folder
# inside it would be a dead line. These three are also named in tools/check_test_inputs.py FIXTURES.
!output/cloud_sky_ground.png
!output/bg_battle_corridor_frame.png
!output/bg_battle_deck_night_frame.png
# The three exterior map frames, the ground the party's four walking sheets are judged on. Card t_dec4e92c,
# 2026-10-25: the three towns' judged rows in data/palettes/scene_southampton.json, scene_westminster.json and
# scene_winchester.json name these by path, and tools/palette_synergy.py --gate fails any row whose ground is not
# on disk, so a clean checkout that lacks them is red with no art to blame. They are written by
# tools/art/make_exterior_maps.py, one per place, and a rerun of that generator reproduces all three byte for
# byte from the committed tileset and OSM drafts (measured on this card), so none of them is a pasted picture.
# They are also named one by one in tools/check_test_inputs.py FIXTURES for the reason the block above gives.
#   output/southampton_sample_frame.png   the 256x240 viewport at Town Quay, spawn tile 17,18
#   output/westminster_sample_frame.png   the viewport at the street by Big Ben, spawn tile 16,20
#   output/winchester_sample_frame.png    the viewport at Winchester High Street, spawn tile 16,19
!output/southampton_sample_frame.png
!output/westminster_sample_frame.png
!output/winchester_sample_frame.png

# The twelve drive captures tests/test_eye_drive.py samples. tools/eye_drive.py reads
# output\drive\pp_drive_shot_01.png to _12.png, which the game writes from inside its own draw
# (pp_drive.gml, PP_DRIVE_CAPTURE), and sample_frames() turns each into the native 256x240 copy
# it measures. Nothing but a GameMaker run produces them, so a clean checkout that lacks them
# reports twelve failed shots. Measured 2026-10-24, card t_d2c52f15: in a detached worktree at
# 75161aa, tests/test_eye_drive.py reported "shots without a captured frame: [1, 2, ... 12]" and
# three reds. These are the files the test measures, not decoration: eye_drive.measure() reads
# each one's own pixels. The pattern is ?? so the derived _1x and _1x_crop files beside them stay
# out, and output/drive/* keeps every other file in that folder out too.
#
# Order and shape matter here. output/* excludes output/drive ITSELF, and git never descends into
# an excluded directory, so a negation for a file inside it would be a dead line. The directory is
# re-included first, then re-excluded wholesale, then the twelve are named.
!output/drive/
output/drive/*
!output/drive/pp_drive_shot_??.png
cache/
